      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes requested** — See inline comments for details. [[trajectory](go/traj/487f5ca5-a726-4108-ade2-d83df54e4407)]\n\n### Review Summary\n\n**Functionality \u0026 Robustness**\n*   **Dead Code:** The CRC32 implementation and `dfu_suffix` struct are unused. If the intent is to validate firmware before flashing, the logic needs to be fully implemented. Otherwise, the dead code should be removed.\n*   **Driver Detachment:** The tool unconditionally detaches the kernel driver from interface `0` instead of the discovered DFU interface, which could cause issues on composite devices.\n*   **Re-enumeration:** Using a fixed `sleep(3)` when waiting for the device to re-enumerate is a potential source of flakiness. A polling approach with a timeout would be much more robust.\n\n**Testing**\n*   As a hardware-interacting host tool, full test coverage might be challenging, but if the CRC32 and argument parsing logic are retained, they should ideally be extracted into testable functions with accompanying unit tests to verify behavior (e.g., ensuring CRC mismatches reject bad firmwares).\n\n**CL Size \u0026 Scope**\n*   The CL is appropriately sized and self-contained.",
