      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Unconditionally detaching the kernel driver from interface `0` might cause unintended side effects, especially if the device is a composite device and the DFU interface is not interface `0`.\n\nIt would be more robust to remove this from `init()` and instead detach the kernel driver from the *actual* DFU interface (`dfu_interface_`) after it has been discovered by `find_dfu_interface()`, just before calling `libusb_claim_interface()` in `dfu_download()`.\n\nFor example, in `dfu_download()`:\n```cpp\nif (libusb_kernel_driver_active(dev_handle_, dfu_interface_) \u003d\u003d 1) {\n    libusb_detach_kernel_driver(dev_handle_, dfu_interface_);\n}\nint ret \u003d libusb_claim_interface(dev_handle_, dfu_interface_);\n```",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "172d58934bd69bb5e9673522cffa3e187d072b65",
