      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Hardcoding a 3-second sleep for USB re-enumeration is prone to races (if the host OS takes longer to enumerate the device) and slows down the happy path.\n\nConsider polling for the device in a loop with a smaller sleep interval (e.g., 100ms) and a timeout (e.g., up to 5-10 seconds). This allows the tool to proceed immediately once the device re-enumerates. \n\n(Note: If you do this, you may want to extract the `libusb_open_device_with_vid_pid` call into a silent polling helper so it does not spam `fprintf` errors during the loop).",
